## minimal config
{
  "api_key": "secret-api_key",
  "server": "https://api.keephq.dev"
}

### down
POST https://api.keephq.dev/alerts/event
X-API-KEY: secret-api_key
(json)
{
  "description": "HTTP 503 (after 3 retries)\nTarget: https://pay.example/health\nType: HTTP(S)\nTime: 2026-10-19 14:03:12 UTC\nhttps://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "fingerprint": "vv-monitor-7",
  "name": "Payments API is down",
  "service": "Payments API",
  "severity": "critical",
  "source": [
    "vigilant-vole"
  ],
  "status": "firing",
  "url": "https://vv.example/monitors/7"
}

### up
POST https://api.keephq.dev/alerts/event
X-API-KEY: secret-api_key
(json)
{
  "description": "down for 12m 4s\nTarget: https://pay.example/health\nType: HTTP(S)\nDowntime: 12m 4s\nTime: 2026-10-19 14:03:12 UTC\nhttps://vv.example/monitors/7",
  "fingerprint": "vv-monitor-7",
  "name": "Payments API is back up",
  "service": "Payments API",
  "severity": "info",
  "source": [
    "vigilant-vole"
  ],
  "status": "resolved",
  "url": "https://vv.example/monitors/7"
}

